**0 — no labels, paired on producer sets.** The unlabelled pair holds no
health document at all, so the label was never *asked* (RFC 09 §5.1 O4);
`web` (`{sysinfo}`) and `db` (`{logs, sysinfo}`) are still told apart by
what they publish, and the note says that is all the pairing rests on.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff --normalize-origins tests/cmd/fixtures/prod-unlabelled.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/stg-unlabelled.zsnap
{"a":{"answered":4,"asked":1,"base":"prod","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:00:00Z","collection_span_s":0.9,"roster":2,"selectors":["prod/v1/**"],"zsnap":1},"b":{"answered":4,"asked":1,"base":"stg","collected_at":"2026-09-06T00:05:00Z","collection_span_s":0.9,"roster":2,"selectors":["stg/v1/**"],"zsnap":1},"notes":[{"cite":"RFC 13 §4.4","text":"a: span 0.90s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.90s at 2026-09-06T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant"},{"cite":"RFC 03 §1.1","text":"b's keys re-based from `stg` onto `prod` for the comparison; the two deployments' clocks are not compared, so a stamp that moved alone is not a change here"},{"cite":"RFC 06 §6.2","text":"2 origin(s) paired by producer set alone — no verified label on both sides; labels ride `state/*/health`, and a snapshot that did not include it never asked for one"}],"origin_map":[{"a":"h-3fa9c2d41b7e","b":"h-c0ffee00c0de","evidence":{"kind":"producer_set"}},{"a":"h-9b2e4c7a1d05","b":"h-0badcafe1234","evidence":{"kind":"producer_set"}}],"report":"snapshot-diff","unchanged":4}
{"compared":1,"differing":0,"only_in_a":0,"only_in_b":0,"row":"subject","subject":"plain/leak"}
{"compared":1,"differing":0,"only_in_a":0,"only_in_b":0,"row":"subject","subject":"state/logs/rotated"}
{"compared":2,"differing":0,"only_in_a":0,"only_in_b":0,"row":"subject","subject":"telemetry/sysinfo/disk/var-log/used"}
a: span 0.90s at 2026-09-06T00:00:00Z, b: span 0.90s at 2026-09-06T00:05:00Z — each side was collected over its span, not at an instant (RFC 13 §4.4)
b's keys re-based from `stg` onto `prod` for the comparison; the two deployments' clocks are not compared, so a stamp that moved alone is not a change here (RFC 03 §1.1)
2 origin(s) paired by producer set alone — no verified label on both sides; labels ride `state/*/health`, and a snapshot that did not include it never asked for one (RFC 06 §6.2)

```

**2 — a `--map` the files do not hold, or one that does not parse.** Both
are the operator's input, refused whole before anything is paired: a plan
that quietly dropped the pairing would compare the wrong keys.

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff --normalize-origins --map h-3fa9c2d41b7e=h-000000000000 tests/cmd/fixtures/prod.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/stg.zsnap
? 2
Error: --map names h-000000000000, which is not a host origin in b

```

```console
$ zenctl snapshot diff --normalize-origins --map web=db tests/cmd/fixtures/prod.zsnap tests/cmd/fixtures/stg.zsnap
? 2
Error: --map "web=db": a is not a host origin (invalid host origin "web": must match h-[0-9a-f]{12} (RFC 03 §1.3))

```
